Subject: [PATCH] capture: distinguish ALSA input and output device identifiers

GstAlsaDeviceProvider reports the same display name for both directions.
Without a PipeWire node.name, microphone lookup can return an alsasink
with the same identifier, leaving the capture pipeline without a source.
Include the device class in fallback IDs; preserve PipeWire identifiers.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerCaptureDeviceManager.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerCaptureDeviceManager.cpp
@@ -224,7 +224,7 @@
     auto label = makeString(isDefault ? "default: "_s : ""_s, deviceName.span());
-
+
     auto nodeName = gstStructureGetString(properties.get(), "node.name"_s);
-    auto identifier = makeString(nodeName.isEmpty() ? deviceName.span() : nodeName);
+    auto identifier = nodeName.isEmpty() ? makeString(deviceClass, ':', deviceName.span()) : makeString(nodeName);
-
+
     bool isMock = false;
     if (auto persistentId = gstStructureGetString(properties.get(), "persistent-id"_s)) {
